{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"9ca2765a-06ff-47e1-bae3-e4a83cc0a5f7","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have identified the issues causing your launchd job to fail silently and implemented the fixes.\n\n### Summary of Causes (documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-tF44M6/ANSWER.md))\n\n1. **`status` is a read-only built-in variable in zsh**:\n   - In [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-tF44M6/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L19), assigning `status=$?` triggered a fatal zsh error (`read-only variable: status`), terminating the script immediately. Because this statement sat right before the failure notification check, the failure reporter never executed.\n2. **Missing `USER` in launchd `EnvironmentVariables`**:\n   - As recorded in [`Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`](file:///tmp/h-tF44M6/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err#L1), the CLI exited with `Not logged in · Please run /login`. Under launchd, user agents run without standard environment variables like `USER`, preventing tools from resolving keychain credentials.\n3. **Multi-line argument handling**:\n   - Multi-line prompts passed directly via command-line arguments in non-interactive/scheduled shells can cause parsing issues or stall awaiting input.\n\n---\n\n### Changes Applied\n\n- **[`Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`](file:///tmp/h-tF44M6/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist#L24-L29)**: Added `USER` (`vk`) to `EnvironmentVariables`.\n- **[`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-tF44M6/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L24)**:\n  - Replaced `status=$?` with `rc=$?` (and updated variable references in the check).\n  - Piped the prompt via stdin using `print -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude -p ...`.\n- **[ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-tF44M6/ANSWER.md)**: Created with a breakdown of each cause and its fix.\n","duration_seconds":55.075282,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":143524,"output_tokens":2534,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":179933,"total_tokens":146058}}}
